---
title: "interestRateModel (Compound Whitepaper)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_get_inputs: getBorrowRate(cash, borrows, reserves) called
    q_get_inputs --> q_calc_util: utilizationRate = borrows / (cash + borrows)
    q_calc_util --> q_calc_borrow: borrowRate = baseRate + utilizationRate * multiplier
    q_calc_borrow --> q_calc_supply: supplyRate = borrowRate * utilizationRate * (1 - reserveFactor)
    q_calc_supply --> [*]: return (borrowRate, supplyRate)

    note right of q_calc_util
        INV-001: utilizationRate in [0, 1]
        INV-002: when cash + borrows = 0, utilizationRate = 0
        INV-003: utilizationRate increases as borrows increase relative to cash
    end note

    note right of q_calc_borrow
        INV-004: borrowRate = baseRate + utilizationRate * multiplier (linear model from whitepaper: 2.5% + U * 20%)
        INV-005: borrowRate >= baseRate (minimum interest rate floor)
        INV-006: borrowRate increases monotonically with utilizationRate
    end note

    note right of q_calc_supply
        INV-007: supplyRate is implicit (borrowRate * utilizationRate * (1 - reserveFactor))
        INV-008: supplyRate <= borrowRate (suppliers earn less due to reserves)
    end note
